msgstr "`VectorReadOps` 或 `MatrixReadOps`"

#: manual/integration/container.md:12
msgid "A source for map, conversion, or transpose"
msgstr "map、转换或转置的输入"

#: manual/integration/container.md:13
msgid "`VectorBuildOps` or `MatrixBuildOps`"
msgstr "`VectorBuildOps` 或 `MatrixBuildOps`"

#: manual/integration/container.md:13
msgid "A target for map, conversion, or transpose"
msgstr "map、转换或转置的输出"

#: manual/integration/container.md:14
msgid "Matching read and build dictionaries"
msgstr "配套的 read 与 build"

#: manual/integration/container.md:14
msgid "Both source and target in generic transformations"
msgstr "泛型变换的输入和输出"

#: manual/integration/container.md:15
msgid "4P"
msgstr "4P"

#: manual/integration/container.md:15
msgid "Persistent edit dictionary"
msgstr "持久编辑字典"

#: manual/integration/container.md:15
msgid "A checked copy-on-replacement value"
msgstr "受检的 copy-on-replacement 值"

#: manual/integration/container.md:16
msgid "4M"
msgstr "4M"

#: manual/integration/container.md:16
msgid "Mutable edit dictionary"
msgstr "可变编辑字典"

#: manual/integration/container.md:16
msgid "A checked in-place update target"
msgstr "受检的原地更新目标"

#: manual/integration/container.md:18
msgid "Levels 4P and 4M are alternatives determined by ownership semantics, not a progression where every backend should implement both. Views commonly provide read plus mutable edit but no build. An append-only or generated container may provide build without read. A foreign handle may intentionally provide read only."
msgstr "4P 与 4M 是由所有权模型决定的替代选择，不是要求所有后端逐级实现两者。视图通常只提供 read 与可变编辑，不提供 build；外部句柄可以只提供 read；生成型容器也可以只提供 build。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:24
msgid "Algorithm requirements"
msgstr "算法要求的能力"

#: manual/integration/container.md:26
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr "算法"

#: manual/integration/container.md:26
msgid "Source requirement"
msgstr "输入要求"

#: manual/integration/container.md:26
msgid "Target requirement"
msgstr "输出要求"

#: manual/integration/container.md:26
msgid "Scalar relationship"
msgstr "标量关系"

#: manual/integration/container.md:28
#: manual/integration/container.md:29
msgid "May change `A` to `B`"
msgstr "可从 `A` 变为 `B`"

#: manual/integration/container.md:30
#: manual/integration/container.md:31
#: manual/integration/container.md:32
msgid "Preserves `T`"
msgstr "保持 `T`"

#: manual/integration/container.md:34
msgid "A read dictionary does not imply construction, editing, arithmetic, contiguous memory, or cheap random access. A build dictionary does not imply that the result can be read back. Edit dictionaries do not imply resizing, insertion, deletion, or sparse-entry removal."
msgstr "read 不代表支持构造、编辑、算术、连续内存或低成本随机访问。build 不代表结果可以读回。编辑字典也不代表 resize、insert、delete 或删除稀疏存储项。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:39
msgid "Mathematical capabilities are independent"
msgstr "数学能力相互独立"

#: manual/integration/container.md:41
msgid "The `algebra` package describes operations such as addition, transpose, and matrix multiplication. The `container` package describes observation and construction. An external type may choose either axis independently:"
msgstr "`algebra` 描述加法、转置和矩阵乘法等数学行为；`container` 描述观察与构造。外部类型可以独立选择这两条能力轴："

#: manual/integration/container.md:45
msgid "Container-only integration supports data movement and structural algorithms without claiming algebraic laws for the scalar or container."
msgstr "只接入 container，可以支持数据移动和结构算法，而无需声明标量或容器的代数定律。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:47
msgid "Algebra-only integration supports closed mathematical operations without exposing individual elements."
msgstr "只接入 algebra，可以在不公开单个元素的情况下提供封闭数学操作。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:49
msgid "Supplying both enables both families of generic algorithms, but one does not automatically satisfy the other."
msgstr "同时提供两者时可以参与两类泛型算法，但任何一方都不会自动推出另一方。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:52
msgid "Do not add broad scalar trait implementations merely to obtain container interoperability. Add mathematical traits only when the type actually provides the documented operation and laws."
msgstr "不要仅为了容器互操作而给标量添加宽泛的全局 trait。只有类型真正满足对应操作与定律时，才实现数学 trait。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:56
msgid "Who owns the adapter"
msgstr "适配器由谁维护"

#: manual/integration/container.md:58
msgid "Prefer the following ownership order:"
msgstr "优先采用以下归属顺序："

#: manual/integration/container.md:60
msgid "The library that owns the container type publishes its operation-dictionary factories when depending on `Luna-Flow/linear-algebra/container` is natural."
msgstr "如果依赖 `Luna-Flow/linear-algebra/container` 是自然的，由容器类型所属库发布操作字典 factory。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:62
msgid "A small bridge package owns the adapters when neither project should depend directly on the other."
msgstr "如果两个项目都不适合直接依赖对方，由一个小型 bridge 包维护适配器。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:64
msgid "`Luna-Flow/linear-algebra` should contain adapters only for implementations maintained in this repository."
msgstr "`Luna-Flow/linear-algebra` 本体只维护本仓库实现的适配器。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:67
msgid "This direction prevents the core package from accumulating optional backend dependencies. Factory names should identify the container and capability, and the factory may carry scalar constraints that are genuinely required by the backend."
msgstr "这一方向可以避免核心包不断累积可选后端依赖。factory 名称应标明容器与能力，factory 也可以携带后端真正需要的标量约束。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:72
msgid "Complete external adapter"
msgstr "完整外部适配器"

#: manual/integration/container.md:74
msgid "This example owns a row-major array, but only the operation dictionaries expose its semantics. The generic transpose targets Luna's immutable matrix type, so the example exercises a real cross-implementation boundary."
msgstr "这个示例拥有行优先数组，但只通过操作字典公开语义。转置目标使用 Luna 的 immutable 矩阵，从而实际验证不同实现之间的边界。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:156
msgid "The backend remains responsible for validating negative dimensions, preserving `0xN` and `Nx0`, reporting invalid coordinates with `LinearAlgebraError`, and honoring its documented ownership behavior."
msgstr "后端仍负责检查负维度、保留 `0xN` 与 `Nx0`、用 `LinearAlgebraError` 报告非法坐标，并遵守自己声明的所有权行为。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:162
msgid "Select only the dictionaries supported by the real storage and ownership model."
msgstr "只选择真实存储和所有权模型支持的字典。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:164
msgid "Keep checked access and construction panic-free."
msgstr "受检访问与构造不得 panic。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:165
msgid "Test first/last and invalid indices, empty and degenerate shapes, and initializer coordinate ordering."
msgstr "测试首尾和非法索引、空与退化形状、initializer 坐标顺序。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:167
msgid "For persistent editing, prove that the source remains unchanged."
msgstr "持久编辑要证明源值保持不变。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:168
msgid "For mutable editing, prove that failure performs no partial mutation."
msgstr "可变编辑要证明失败时不会发生部分修改。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:169
msgid "Test at least one generic map or conversion in both supported directions."
msgstr "对每个支持的方向至少测试一次泛型 map 或转换。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:170
msgid "Document performance characteristics such as remote access, decompression, or sparse materialization costs without changing the semantic contract."
msgstr "记录远程访问、解压或稀疏 materialization 等性能特征，但不要改变语义契约。"

#: manual/integration/container.md:173
msgid "Future optimized kernel dictionaries should be additional opt-in capabilities. They must not become prerequisites for read/build interoperability."
msgstr "未来的优化 kernel 字典应是额外的 opt-in 能力，不能成为 read/build 互操作的前提。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:1
msgid "algebra tutorial"
msgstr "algebra 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:5
msgid "If you want to use the abstract linear-algebra layers directly, install the full dependency set first:"
msgstr "如果你想直接使用抽象线性代数能力层，先把完整依赖装好："

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:25
msgid "This gives you one clear split: `@algebra` for linear-algebra structure traits, `@la_arithmetic` for linear-algebra-facing operation traits, `@lf_alg` for the shared upstream algebraic abstractions, and `@lf_arith` for upstream arithmetic types."
msgstr "这样分工会很清楚：`@algebra` 负责线性代数结构 trait，`@la_arithmetic` 负责线性代数操作 trait，`@lf_alg` 负责共享上游代数抽象，`@lf_arith` 负责共享上游算术类型。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:30
msgid "Small case: build one backend-independent Gram step"
msgstr "小案例：构造一个与后端无关的 Gram 步骤"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:54
msgid "This case shows how to describe a backend-independent linear-algebra step in terms of the structure traits owned by this package:"
msgstr "这个例子展示了，怎样只用本包拥有的线性代数结构 trait 来表达一个与后端无关的步骤："

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:57
msgid "Require `MatMulMatrix` so the algorithm can multiply one matrix-like value by another."
msgstr "用 `MatMulMatrix` 说明算法确实需要矩阵式乘法。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:58
msgid "Reuse `TransposeMatrix` through the `MatMulMatrix` hierarchy instead of naming a dense backend API directly."
msgstr "通过 `MatMulMatrix` 继承到的 `TransposeMatrix` 能力调用转置，而不是直接写死某个稠密后端 API。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:59
msgid "Ask `MatrixShape` for the result shape without depending on storage layout."
msgstr "用 `MatrixShape` 读取结果形状，不依赖具体存储形式。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:60
msgid "Run the same helper on a real default backend wrapper to confirm the trait contract is practical, not just abstract."
msgstr "最后拿真实的默认后端包装类型跑一遍，确认这些 trait 不只是抽象命名，而是能直接承载实际能力。"

#: manual/tutorial/algebra.md:62
msgid "The result stays generic while still expressing a recognizably linear-algebraic operation."
msgstr "这样写出来的算法既保留了线代语义，也不会被某个具体后端绑定住。"

